ry matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 14 & -5\\end{aligned}] & \\,{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058701/state.json" "file_sha256" "0cb6e4900c271401c47fe4bb90f001e1935a8eb6bd27e69f260e4847c8b72e5d"} {"question" "q-106765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e0e5c10da6ead45c0e8bd01f0506e038c195bfddc01dae4e7fb2063d729afef"} {"question" "q-106765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058701/state.json" "file_sha256" "0cb6e4900c271401c47fe4bb90f001e1935a8eb6bd27e69f260e4847c8b72e5d"} {"question" "q-106765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{alig